A||||5||nova||need help with front end!!!
Z||000000||nova||07-15-99||03:59 PM||||<br>i just picked up a 1987 fiero, and the driver's side front tire is not strait, the bottom is kicking out, i don't no if it's the ball joint or tie rod end, or something worse, i no it needs outer tie rods, the rpm gauge doesn't work either, everything looks hooked up, i wonder if anyone ever had this happen before i tear the car apart.
Z||000001||four50four||07-15-99||04:11 PM||||does it have a tach filter?
Z||000002||vurbanson||07-15-99||04:43 PM||||Hey, my tach died on me a couple of times too.  It turned out it was the plug on top of the ignition coil (double plug - black and grey).  It was loose and cutting out.  Sometimes it seems like it's fine because it's plugged in - wrong! One of the plugs could be plugged in but because they're sort of attached, you won't know if one is not.  Check the connection on it.  Unless it's in your gauge, it's got nothing to do with mechanicals - it's electrical.
Z||000003||lowCG||07-15-99||04:54 PM||||The Tach Filter is a condenser,I believe,is there to suppress spikes that'll make the tach twitch; it can short out,internally with age.<br>Usually located near the coil.<br>Sounds like your front end needs about $200-$300 worth of parts,and a weekend.<br>Suspension Technology has everything except the bushings for the best prices,need to talk to ext.352,though;no one else seems to know that they have any parts left for the Fiero.
Z||000004||batboy||07-15-99||05:51 PM||||If the bottom of the tire angles out compared to the top of the tire, it could be bad ball joints or the front end severely out of alignment or both. Most high mileage Fieros will have at least some wear in the ball joints, many have a lot of wear.
Z||000005||Cooter||07-15-99||06:34 PM||||When I bought my 85 SE the left front tire was really in at the top- or out at the bottom- the car was sitting low on that corner because the tire was in so much at the top. I thought the spring had went soft but it turned out that the "frame rails" had settled in at the top on both sides and had to be tied on the frame machine and stretched out at the top of the a-arms to correct the awkward tire angle. Thank goodnes I work in a body shop!
